==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=cassette}}

===Etymology===
{{borrowing|fr|lang=en}} ''[[#French|cassette]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kəˈsɛt/|/kæˈsɛt/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɛt}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A small flat case containing [[magnetic tape]] on two [[reel]]s, used to [[record]] and [[play back]] [[audio]] and [[video]] material.
# Any similar small [[cartridge]], such as for a computer disk.
# {{context|photography|lang=en}} A lightproof container for photographic [[film]].
# {{context|genetics|lang=en}} A [[modular]] DNA [[sequence]] encoding one or more genes for a single biochemical function.
# A set of [[sprocket]]s mounted onto a [[splined]] [[shaft]] on the [[freehub]].

